  "question": {
    "text": "Let $a, b$ and $c$ be distinct non-negative numbers. If the vectors $a \\hat{i}+a \\hat{j}+c \\hat{k}, \\hat{i}+\\hat{k}$ and $c \\hat{i}+c \\hat{j}+b \\hat{k}$ lie in a plane, then $c$ is",
    "image": null
  },
  "options": [
    {
      "id": "jEMUF",
      "text": "\nthe Geometric Mean of $a$ and $b$\n",
      "image": null,
      "isCorrect": true
    },
    {
      "id": "Y8oOf",
      "text": "\nthe Arithmetic Mean of $a$ and $b$\n",
      "image": null,
      "isCorrect": false
    },
    {
      "id": "iMPTU",
      "text": "\nequal to zero\n",
      "image": null,
      "isCorrect": false
    },
    {
      "id": "330J2",
      "text": "\nthe Harmonic Mean of $a$ and $b$",
      "image": null,
      "isCorrect": false
    }
  ],
  "correctValue": null,
  "solution": {
    "text": "Vector $a \\hat{i}+a \\hat{j}+c \\hat{k}, \\hat{i}+\\hat{k}$ and $c \\hat{i}+c \\hat{j}+b \\hat{k}$ are coplanar\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n& \\left|\\begin{array}{lll}\na & a & c \\\\\n1 & 0 & 1 \\\\\nc & c & b\n\\end{array}\\right|=0 \\Rightarrow c^2=a b \\\\\n& \\therefore a, b, c \\text { are in G.P. }\n\\end{aligned}\n$$",
    "image": null
  },
